            <div xml:id="d938">

                <pb facs="0961" n="949" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg949"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8837: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-06T18:00:00+01:00">March 6, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. For the Under Secretary. I learn from a reliable source that Fotić who is
                    one of the most highly regarded Yugoslav diplomatic representatives has been
                    telegraphing fully his conversations with you and that these reports have had an
                    excellent effect in fortifying attitude of high officials here. It has been
                    suggested to me that the more ammunition you can give him the more efficacious
                    the results will be here.</p>
                <p>As I know that you are on close terms with Fotić I am not forwarding the
                    foregoing as a suggestion, but merely for your information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
